From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] user32: Implement EndTask.

Adopted from LinDobe (le-birnes/LinDobe, LGPL-2.1+), patch 0100, with these changes: code unchanged; the win.c hunk placed by hand after TileChildWindows (our win.c has more code after it, so the
original hunk only applied with fuzz 2), the user32.spec line as in the original.

AdobeCollabSync calls it and Wine's stub aborted the process ("unimplemented function user32.dll.EndTask").
EndTask sends WM_CLOSE; with force it ends the process when the window stays.
Test: wine/tests/endtask: bad window, window closes, no force leaves it, force ends the process.

Lab (acrobat-adopt, 2026-11-08, runtime 11.10-185ad = 185 + riched20-textpara-getters + unsecapp-wmi-sink-host
+ this set): Acrobat Pro installed the user's way (`neutron programs install` of the Acrobat setup.exe = AcroPro.msi +
AcrobatDCx64Upd2600222031.msp) into a fresh copy of a signed-in Adobe prefix: "Setup Completed", installed 26.002.22031,
7778 files, 1.8 GB, thorvg-1.dll present (n=1). Before this set every install ended 1603 at PatchFiles (AcMsp-1..9).
Lab: Acrobat 26.002 relaunch aborted with "unimplemented function user32.dll.EndTask" on 185 + the set without this
(log acrobat-pgi-ad1-20261108-210658.log); with it, no EndTask abort in 4 later launches.
Kill switch: none.
---
--- a/dlls/user32/user32.spec
+++ b/dlls/user32/user32.spec
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@
 @ stdcall EndDialog(long long)
 @ stdcall EndMenu() NtUserEndMenu
 @ stdcall EndPaint(long ptr) NtUserEndPaint
-@ stub EndTask
+@ stdcall EndTask(long long long)
 # @ stub EnterReaderModeHelper
 @ stdcall EnumChildWindows(long ptr long)
 @ stdcall EnumClipboardFormats(long) NtUserEnumClipboardFormats
--- a/dlls/user32/win.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/win.c
@@ -2253,6 +2253,35 @@
 }
 
 /**********************************************************************
+ *              EndTask (USER32.@)
+ *
+ * Asks a window to close; with force, ends its process when the window stays.
+ */
+BOOL WINAPI EndTask( HWND hwnd, BOOL shutdown, BOOL force )
+{
+    DWORD_PTR result;
+    DWORD pid = 0;
+    HANDLE process;
+    BOOL ret;
+
+    TRACE( "%p %d %d\n", hwnd, shutdown, force );
+
+    if (!GetWindowThreadProcessId( hwnd, &pid ))
+    {
+        SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_WINDOW_HANDLE );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+    SendMessageTimeoutW( hwnd, WM_CLOSE, 0, 0, SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, 5000, &result );
+    if (!IsWindow( hwnd )) return TRUE;
+    if (!force) return FALSE;
+
+    if (!(process = OpenProcess( PROCESS_TERMINATE, FALSE, pid ))) return FALSE;
+    ret = TerminateProcess( process, 0 );
+    CloseHandle( process );
+    return ret;
+}
+
